    <text><list><item>First prenatal visit: blood count, ferritin, quantitative hCG, blood group and antibody screen, rubella immunity, hepatitis B surface antigen, HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis C tests; urine culture; influenza vaccine; prenatal vitamin with folic acid. Guideline: USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Guidelines for Vaccinating Pregnant Persons (2026) [S]</item><item>Nausea and vomiting: small, frequent, bland meals, ginger, and doxylamine with pyridoxine at bedtime; return for vomiting that stops her keeping fluids down, weight loss, or dizziness. Guideline: ACOG Practice Bulletin No. 189: Nausea and Vomiting of Pregnancy (2018) [S]</item><item>Iron deficiency anemia: ferrous sulfate 325 mg every other day; blood count and ferritin at the anatomy-scan visit, with intravenous iron in the second trimester if there is no response. Guideline: Anemia in Pregnancy: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 233 (2021) [S]</item><item>Mood: EPDS in each trimester and after the birth. Guideline: Screening and Diagnosis of Mental Health Conditions During Pregnancy and Postpartum: ACOG Clinical Practice Guideline No. 4 (2023) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to maternal-fetal medicine, Samira Haddad-Thornbury, MD, ordered 2026-03-03 [S]</item></list></text>

